# Post-deploy & backward-compat checklist

Maintain `to_migrate.md` at the repo root for work the deployer must do **after** (or in a specific order with) the code going live.

**Non-negotiable:** If a change needs backward compatibility handling, a coordinated deploy order, or anything production will not pick up from a plain code deploy — append it to `to_migrate.md` in the same turn as the code change. Do not leave it only in chat or commit messages.

## Format

Checkboxes only. One line each: the command, env var, or deploy note, then a short dash description.

```
# To migrate

- [ ] `cd backend && npx prisma migrate deploy` — Apply pending Prisma migrations
- [ ] Set `DIGEST_CRON` in backend `.env` — Daily digest schedule (cron)
- [ ] Deploy backend before frontend — API field `foo` required by new UI
```

No essays, file lists, or implementation notes.

## When to append

After a change that production will not pick up from the deploy alone, **or** that breaks / risks breaking an older client, older server, or existing data:

- A Prisma migration that needs `migrate deploy`
- A new, renamed, or removed `.env` variable
- A one-off command (seed, backfill, restart a worker)
- **Backward compatibility / breaking change**, including:
  - Deploy order (e.g. migrate DB before code, backend before frontend)
  - Backfill or data rewrite so old rows keep working
  - Dual-read / dual-write period that ops must enable or tear down
  - API or payload shape change that old clients cannot ignore
  - Enum / column rename or drop that needs a sequenced migration
  - Storage path, upload, or cache invalidation step after cutover

Skip if the same unchecked item is already on the list. Do not log local-only steps (`migrate dev`, `prisma generate`, `npm install`).

## When to check off

Only when the user confirms it was done on the deployed environment. Do not tick boxes after a local run or a git commit.

If every item is checked, reset to:

```
# To migrate

(none)
```
